diff --git a/features/todo-editing.feature b/features/todo-editing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e37b9d1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+@logic
+Feature: Todo editing
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todos
+  So that I can correct or update task descriptions
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+    And the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: Entering edit mode
+
+  Scenario: Activate editing mode on double-click
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    Then the li for "Buy milk" should have the editing class
+    And the edit input should be focused
+
+  Scenario: Hide todo controls during editing
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    Then the view controls for "Buy milk" should be hidden
+    And the edit input for "Buy milk" should be visible
+
+  Rule: Saving edits
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on Enter key
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit input value to "Buy organic milk" and press Enter
+    Then I should see "Buy organic milk" in the todo list
+    And the li for "Buy organic milk" should not have the editing class
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on blur
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit input value to "Buy organic milk" and blur
+    Then I should see "Buy organic milk" in the todo list
+    And the li for "Buy organic milk" should not have the editing class
+
+  Scenario: Trim whitespace on save
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit input value to "  Buy organic milk  " and press Enter
+    Then I should see "Buy organic milk" in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Destroy todo when edit value is empty
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit input value to "" and press Enter
+    Then the todo list should be empty
+
+  Scenario: Destroy todo when edit value is whitespace only
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit input value to "   " and press Enter
+    Then the todo list should be empty
+
+  Rule: Cancelling edits
+
+  Scenario: Cancel edit on Escape key
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit input value to "Buy organic milk" and press Escape
+    Then I should see "Buy milk" in the todo list
+    And the li for "Buy milk" should not have the editing class
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-management.feature b/features/todo-management.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c870907
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-management.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+@logic
+Feature: Todo management
+  As a user
+  I want to manage a list of todos
+  So that I can keep track of tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Adding todos
+
+  Scenario: Create a new todo by pressing Enter
+    Given the input field is empty
+    When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then I should see "Buy milk" in the todo list
+    And the input field should be cleared
+
+  Scenario: Trim whitespace from new todo title
+    Given the input field is empty
+    When I type "   Learn TodoMVC   " into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then I should see "Learn TodoMVC" in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Reject empty todo on Enter
+    Given the input field is empty
+    When I press Enter on the new-todo input
+    Then the todo list should be empty
+
+  Scenario: Reject whitespace-only todo on Enter
+    Given the input field is empty
+    When I type "   " into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list should be empty
+
+  Rule: Listing todos
+
+  Scenario: Hide main and footer when there are no todos
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    Then the main section should be hidden
+    And the footer should be hidden
+
+  Scenario: Show main and footer when a todo exists
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    When I add a todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the main section should be visible
+    And the footer should be visible
+
+  Rule: Completing todos
+
+  Scenario: Mark a todo as complete
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I check the toggle for "Buy milk"
+    Then "Buy milk" should have the completed class
+
+  Scenario: Unmark a completed todo
+    Given "Buy milk" is completed
+    When I uncheck the toggle for "Buy milk"
+    Then "Buy milk" should not have the completed class
+
+  Rule: Deleting todos
+
+  Scenario: Delete a todo via destroy button
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I click the destroy button for "Buy milk"
+    Then I should not see "Buy milk" in the todo list
+
+  Rule: Toggling all todos
+
+  Scenario: Mark all todos as complete
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos should be completed
+
+  Scenario: Mark all todos as active when toggle-all is unchecked
+    Given all todos are completed
+    When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos should be active
+
+  Scenario: Update toggle-all checkbox when individual toggles complete all
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When I check the toggle for "Buy milk"
+    And I check the toggle for "Walk the dog"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox should be checked
+
+  Scenario: Update toggle-all checkbox when individual uncheck leaves incomplete
+    Given all todos are completed
+    When I uncheck the toggle for "Buy milk"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox should not be checked
+
+  Rule: Counter
+
+  Scenario: Display count of active todos with pluralization
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And "Walk the dog" is completed
+    Then the todo-count should show "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Display pluralized count for zero active todos
+    Given "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog" are completed
+    Then the todo-count should show "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Display pluralized count for multiple active todos
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    Then the todo-count should show "2 items left"
+
+  Rule: Clear completed
+
+  Scenario: Remove completed todos on clear completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    And "Buy milk" is completed
+    When I click the clear-completed button
+    Then I should not see "Buy milk" in the todo list
+    And I should see "Walk the dog" in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Hide clear-completed button when no completed todos exist
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the page loads
+    Then the clear-completed button should be hidden
+
+  Scenario: Show clear-completed button when a completed todo exists
+    Given "Buy milk" is completed
+    Then the clear-completed button should be visible
+
+  Scenario: Clear checked state of toggle-all after clear completed
+    Given all todos are completed
+    When I click the clear-completed button
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox should not be checked
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-persistence.feature b/features/todo-persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..de9045e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+@logic
+Feature: Todo persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Saving todos to localStorage
+
+  Scenario: Persist todos in localStorage after adding
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    When I add a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage should contain a todo with title "Buy milk"
+    And the todo should have keys "id", "title", and "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Persist completed state in localStorage
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I check the toggle for "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" in localStorage should have completed set to true
+
+  Scenario: Persist active state in localStorage
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" in localStorage should have completed set to false
+
+  Scenario: Remove todo from localStorage on delete
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I click the destroy button for "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage should not contain a todo with title "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: Restoring todos from localStorage
+
+  Scenario: Restore todos after page reload
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then I should see "Buy milk" in the todo list
+    And I should see "Walk the dog" in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Restore completion state after page reload
+    Given "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then "Buy milk" should have the completed class
+
+  Rule: Editing state
+
+  Scenario: Do not persist editing state
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then no todo should have the editing class
+
+  Scenario: Use correct localStorage key
+    Then the localStorage key should be "todos-vanilla"
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-routing.feature b/features/todo-routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..22a929f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+@logic
+Feature: Todo routing and filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter todos by completion state
+  So that I can focus on active or completed tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+    And the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    And "Buy milk" is completed
+
+  Rule: All route
+
+  Scenario: Show all todos on #/ route
+    Given the URL hash is "#/"
+    Then I should see "Buy milk" in the filtered list
+    And I should see "Walk the dog" in the filtered list
+    And the All filter link should have the selected class
+
+  Rule: Active route
+
+  Scenario: Show only active todos on #/active route
+    Given the URL hash is "#/active"
+    Then I should see "Walk the dog" in the filtered list
+    And I should not see "Buy milk" in the filtered list
+    And the Active filter link should have the selected class
+
+  Rule: Completed route
+
+  Scenario: Show only completed todos on #/completed route
+    Given the URL hash is "#/completed"
+    Then I should see "Buy milk" in the filtered list
+    And I should not see "Walk the dog" in the filtered list
+    And the Completed filter link should have the selected class
+
+  Rule: Default route
+
+  Scenario: Default to all route on no hash
+    Given the URL hash is ""
+    Then I should see "Buy milk" in the filtered list
+    And I should see "Walk the dog" in the filtered list
+
+  Rule: Filtered state updates
+
+  Scenario: Hide completed todo when checked in active filter
+    Given the URL hash is "#/active"
+    When I check the toggle for "Walk the dog"
+    Then I should not see "Walk the dog" in the filtered list
+
+  Scenario: Hide active todo when unchecked in completed filter
+    Given the URL hash is "#/completed"
+    When I uncheck the toggle for "Buy milk"
+    Then I should not see "Buy milk" in the filtered list
+
+  Rule: Persisting filter on reload
+
+  Scenario: Restore active filter on page reload
+    Given the URL hash is "#/active"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the Active filter link should have the selected class
\ No newline at end of file
